course: dictionary
lesson: 9751
title: Supernova: a star's final blaze
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A supernova is a word for a star's huge explosion at the end of its life. You can find its meaning from the words around it. «Stars more than about 8 times as heavy as the Sun end in a supernova, an explosion that for weeks can outshine a whole galaxy.» Outshine means shine much brighter than, so a supernova is a very bright explosion.
explain: The sentence also tells you what is happening: the star is dying. «Betelgeuse... is a dying red supergiant that will explode as a supernova.» So a supernova is the blast that comes when a dying star explodes. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Explosion fits, so your meaning works.
explain: Look at the clue «like a firework that briefly lights up a whole city». A firework is a bright burst of light that lasts only a moment, so a supernova is a sudden, dazzling flash. The picture in your head helps you remember the word.
fact: A supernova (plural supernovae) is a gigantic explosion of a star at the end of its life.
fact: A supernova can shine brighter than a whole galaxy for a short time.
fact: Stars more than about 8 times as heavy as the Sun end their lives in a supernova.
fact: After a supernova, a neutron star about 20 kilometres across or a black hole may be left behind.
fact: Supernovae spread elements like iron and gold into space, so the atoms in our bodies were made in stars.
exercise: «Stars more than about 8 times as heavy as the Sun end in a supernova, an explosion that for weeks can outshine a whole galaxy.» What does outshine mean? | Grow colder than | Hide behind | Weigh more than | *Shine much brighter than
exercise: What does supernova mean? | *A gigantic explosion of a star at the end of its life | A type of firework for Bonfire Night | A tiny, cold moon | A group of stars that never change
exercise: «Betelgeuse, Orion's red shoulder, is a dying red supergiant that will explode as a supernova sometime within about the next 100,000 years.» Find and copy one word that means ending its life. | *dying | shoulder | sometime | Orion's
test: «A supernova was seen from Earth in 1054 and made the Crab Nebula.» What did the supernova make? | The Moon | *The Crab Nebula | A small galaxy next to ours | A red supergiant
test: «In February 1987 a supernova... became visible to the naked eye from the southern hemisphere, though not from northern lands like Britain.» Why could people in Britain not see it easily? | The supernova had already faded away | *Britain is in the northern hemisphere, where it could not be seen | The star was too bright to look at | Their telescopes were broken
exam: Jayden says a supernova is a small, quiet star. Using the clue «an explosion that for weeks can outshine a whole galaxy», what is wrong with his idea? | Stars never explode, so there is no problem with his idea | It is a kind of cloud that hides stars | It is a small planet that orbits the Sun | *It is a huge, bright explosion, not a small, quiet star
